      "testOnly": true,
      "rationale": "A second implementation of the `s.raster.raster` layered document and all twelve typed mutations, in Python, at `../🧪️tests/🟠️mutate-raster-1/🐍️.py`. Written from `../🧬️schema/🧬️mutations/🔣️.json` (all twelve variants, their internally tagged wire form and each one's required members), `../🧬️schema/🧬️mutations/📝️text/📖️.grammar.semio` (the twelve verbs and their positional argument lists) and the twelve committed `(before, mutation, after, outcome)` specification vectors. It imports nothing from this repository and transliterates none of its Rust. A third-party library was declined, not merely absent: `png`, `image` and `tiff` read image FILES and this artifact is a layer tree over an id-keyed asset pool; Pillow reads the pixel payloads and has no authority over a group's `children`, a blend mode, or a reorder that lifts a node out of a group. What a reference can adjudicate is the tree algebra, and that is what this one implements. DEFECT FOUND WHILE WRITING IT, reported rather than worked around: `../🧬️schema/📸️snapshot/🔣️.json` does not describe this artifact — it is a verbatim copy of `s.stdio.json`'s `JsonSnapshot` schema with the wrong `$id`, so the mutation schema's `RasterLayerNode` reference points at nothing; the document shape was read off the twelve committed vectors, which agree with one another on every field. `package` is deliberately empty: the implementation needs no distribution, so this entry contributes nothing to `🔒️dependencies.json`.\n\nUNDER PROTOCOL V2 this registration is classified `cross-semio-implementation` — a required SUPPLEMENTAL oracle that does not discharge `raster-1-mutate`'s external-oracle requirement for its 12-kind mutation vocabulary; a qualifying third-party reference (`third-party-library` / `third-party-cli` / `standards-reference-tool`) is still owed.\n\n[2026-09-02, D1 — SEPARATE-ARTIFACT-STANDARD-SUBSET-IMPLEMENTATIONS-AND-FIXTURE-TEST-EVERY-MUTATION] Promoted from cross-semio-implementation to verified-native-second-implementation: this artifact is semio-native (isSemioNativeArtifact), this reference's own third-party survey above (kept verbatim) already names what was checked and declined, its python implementation differs from the Rust subject, and it covers 100% of this manifest's 1 capability/capabilities with 12 committed fixture vector(s). See .🧬semio/🦑️repo/🎫️tickets/🎆️26/🌙️09/☀️02/SEPARATE-ARTIFACT-STANDARD-SUBSET-IMPLEMENTATIONS-AND-FIXTURE-TEST-EVERY-MUTATION/📓️d1-native-oracle-discharge.md.",
